---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = "Resources & Videos | AOC, Calgary";
const description = "Browse Canadian mental health information, substance use education, professional videos and Alberta support resources.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
<main id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="wrap"><section class="page-head"><div class="eyebrow">The learning space</div><h1>Understanding starts<br>with good questions.</h1><p class="lead">A small, considered collection of mental health and substance use information from established Canadian organizations.</p></section><section class="resources"><div class="cards"><article class="resource-card"><div class="eyebrow">READ / CAMH</div><h3>Understand mental health & addiction</h3><p>Accessible overviews of mental health conditions, substances, and treatment topics from the Centre for Addiction and Mental Health.</p><a class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.camh.ca/en/health-info/mental-illness-and-addiction-index">Browse the health library ↗</a></article><article class="resource-card"><div class="eyebrow">EXPLORE / CCSA</div><h3>A clearer view of substance use</h3><p>Research and educational resources from the Canadian Centre on Substance Use and Addiction.</p><a class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.ccsa.ca/en">Explore substance use resources ↗</a></article><article class="resource-card"><div class="eyebrow">LOCAL SUPPORT / ALBERTA</div><h3>Find support closer to home</h3><p>An Alberta directory of addiction and mental health services, information, and support options.</p><a class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.albertahealthservices.ca/amh/amh.aspx">Find Alberta services ↗</a></article></div><div class="resource-video"><div class="eyebrow">WATCH / CCSA · For professionals & learners</div><h2>What supports good<br>substance use care?</h2><p>CCSA’s Competencies Video Series introduces the knowledge, skills, and behaviours that support work with people who use substances.</p><a class="btn outline" href="https://competencies.ccsa.ca/en/understanding-competencies/competencies-video-series" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Watch the video series ↗</a></div><p class="small" style="margin-top:28px">These links open external websites. Content belongs to the named organizations; inclusion does not imply an affiliation or endorsement of AOC. Resources provide general education, not personalized advice. Original AOC videos have not yet been published.</p></section></div></main>
</Layout>
